<section class="about-section" data-nav-theme="light">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="about-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--blue)">Why this study matters</p>
        <h2>Nigerian dentistry has no comprehensive workforce data.</h2>
        <p>Decisions about dental education, regulation, remuneration, and practice policy are being made without reliable, current evidence. The workforce challenges Nigerian dentists face — from compensation to working conditions to the pressures that drive emigration — are poorly documented.</p>
        <p>This study changes that. By capturing the direct experiences of practising dentists across Nigeria, the Dentistry Workforce Study 2026 will produce the first systematic evidence base for the profession — one that APDPN and other stakeholders can use to advocate effectively on your behalf.</p>
        <p>The findings will be published as the <strong>Nigerian Dentistry Workforce Report 2026</strong>, freely available to all participants and the broader dental community.</p>
      </div>
